Statement. U_A is the relaxation bound for 316 full measurements on the clock grid, each instant at most once: it bounds every scheme whose per-step information weights are each <= 1 and sum to <= 316. Send-on-delta is not such a scheme: with 316.9 sends its weights sum to 465.96, because the non-send steps carry censoring information. U_A is therefore not a limit for send-on-delta. U_B (weights each <= 1, total equal to send-on-delta's own S(u)) is the relaxation that does contain send-on-delta's weight pattern at this input.

